; Sprite draw queue: 16 jobs of 16 bytes
;
; Jobs for drawing sprites into the redraw buffers. #R$9836 and #R$97FD, run from the frame call list, fill a template
; and #R$98B1 appends a copy at the end of the queue (the tail address is the operand of its first instruction).
; #R$97B7 then walks the queue (#R$97E1): for each job whose first word is not zero it calls the routine at that
; address with DE = job + 1 and clears the word, so the queue is empty again afterwards and the first word is also the
; marker of a free job. Fields: +0 word routine ($9972 for a masked sprite, $98F7 for an object sprite), the other 14
; bytes are the parameters of the routine (#R$98D9 and #R$982E list them). A 17th job would run into the object slots
; at #R$C100.
@label=DrawQueue
g$C000 DEFS $0100,$FF ;
